docs {
  # Get Current User

  Returns the currently authenticated user's details.

  ## Authentication
  Requires a valid access token in the `Authorization` header:
  ```
  Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
  ```

  ## Request
  No parameters required.

  ## Response
  Returns the authenticated user with roles and permissions.

  ## Example Response
  ```json
  {
    "user": {
      "id": "uuid",
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "name": "John Doe",
      "roles": [
        {
          "id": "uuid",
          "name": "viewer",
          "permissions": [
            {
              "id": "uuid",
              "name": "entry.read",
              "resource": "entry",
              "action": "read"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": "2026-03-27T18:40:15+01:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-03-27T18:40:15+01:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  - `UNAUTHENTICATED`: not authenticated or invalid token
  - `NOT_FOUND`: user not found
}
